      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**The issue:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5100 mg/day**. That's twice the maximum labeled dose:\n- Immediate-release metformin: max **2550 mg/day** (e.g., 850 mg three times daily)\n- Extended-release metformin: max **2000 mg/day**\n\nAbove these doses, the risk of GI side effects and lactic acidosis goes up, and blood sugar control doesn't improve.\n\n**Some common orders it may have been meant as:**\n1. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum). This may be a mix-up between 850 mg and 1700 mg.\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg by mouth twice daily with meals.\n3. **Metformin 1000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (2000 mg/day, a common target dose).\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me the correct dose, and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily for a specific reason, please confirm that and give the reason. I'll put it in the order note so pharmacy can see it when they review."
      }
     ],
